"Usage: zenoh_publisher [OPTIONS]\n\nOptions:\n  -e, --endpoint <ENDPOINT>\n          The endpoint for Zenoh client to connect to [default: tcp/127.0.0.1:7447]\n      --zenoh-config <ZENOH_CONFIG>\n          Optional Zenoh JSON5 configuration file. When set, this overrides --endpoint\n      --uauthority <UAUTHORITY>\n          Authority for the local publisher identity and publish source URI [default: authority-b]\n      --uentity <UENTITY>\n          UEntity ID for publish source URI (decimal or 0x-prefixed hex) [default: 0x13039]\n      --uversion <UVERSION>\n          UEntity major version for publish source URI (decimal or 0x-prefixed hex) [default: 0x1]\n      --resource <RESOURCE>\n          Resource ID for publish source URI (decimal or 0x-prefixed hex) [default: 0x8001]\n      --send-count <SEND_COUNT>\n          Number of publish messages to send before exiting (0 means run forever) [default: 0]\n      --send-interval-ms <SEND_INTERVAL_MS>\n          Milliseconds to wait between publish sends [default: 1000]\n      --route-family <ROUTE_FAMILY>\n          Optional selected-wire route family. Omit this flag to use the classic UTransport example path [possible values: owned-frame, copy-minimized]\n      --encoding <ENCODING>\n          Payload encoding used when --route-family selects a selected-wire path [default: protobuf] [possible values: native, protobuf, xcdrv2, arrow, omgidl]\n      --payload <PAYLOAD>\n          Text payload used by selected-wire examples [default: zenoh-publisher]\n      --selected-send-count <SELECTED_SEND_COUNT>\n          Number of selected-wire payloads to send before exiting [default: 1]\n      --payload-alignment <PAYLOAD_ALIGNMENT>\n          Payload alignment for non-native copy-minimized sends [default: 1]\n  -h, --help\n          Print help\n  -V, --version\n          Print version\n"
